// Shared shapes for Subtitle E chapters 52 (tobacco), 53 (firearms/NFA), 54
// (greenmail) and 55 (structured settlement factoring) — this package owns
// all of Subtitle E except chapter 51 (alcohol, its own package). Method per
// AGENT-BRIEF: every excise imposed here is a calculation over a taxable
// EVENT (removal, transfer, making, receipt) with the liable person captured
// as an institutional effect. `us.irc.excise_goods` already declares the
// shared top type and the two relations every excise family bridges into
// (`ExciseEvent`, `excise_tax_due`, `liable_for_excise`, `tax_free_sale`);
// this package imports them rather than mirroring a lookalike, per
// AGENT-BRIEF's "you MAY import us.irc.excise_goods 0.1.0 only if a shared
// shape is pub and fits" — it fits: a tobacco removal, an NFA transfer/
// making, a greenmail receipt and a structured-settlement factoring
// transaction are all "tax imposed on an event" in exactly the shape
// `00-shared.law` of `excise-goods` describes.
//
// JUDGMENT CALL (report this): `us.irc.core::liability` is keyed by ANNUAL
// TaxableYear; chapter 52 tobacco excise is determined at removal and paid
// on a SEMIMONTHLY return period (section 5703(b)), and chapter 53 NFA
// transfer/making taxes are paid per transaction via stamp (section
// 5811(c)/5821(c)), neither of which is annual. Same class of gap as
// `excise-goods`' own `pending_core_extension` dependency row — this
// package stops at the per-event `liable_for_excise` relation and does not
// bridge into `us.irc.core::liability`.

type Person = us.irc.core::Person;
type Organ = us.irc.core::Organ;

const Secretary: Organ = us.irc.core::Secretary;
const DistrictCourt: Organ = us.irc.core::DistrictCourt;

type ExciseEvent = us.irc.excise_goods::ExciseEvent;

// `excise_tax_due`, `liable_for_excise` and `tax_free_sale` are used
// throughout this package by their full `us.irc.excise_goods::` path
// (no local alias declared — a relation cannot be re-exported under a
// second name the way a type can; see CONTRACT.md's naming-convention note).
